From 5795d68e43110a19de2b71fec1028a623dd3ff3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leopold Li <leopold.lixiaoliang@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 17:15:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] feat(gateway): ACK queued messages during busy session
 (queue mode UX)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem
-------
When ``busy_input_mode: queue`` (WeChat DM default), a follow-up sent
during an active turn used to be silently queued — no immediate reply,
no receipt confirmation. User has no idea the bot received the message
until the current turn finishes and the queued message eventually gets
processed. Feels like "did the bot get it?".

Fix
---
Add a short ACK send when ``_handle_active_session_busy_message`` hits
the queue branch:

  * New helper ``_maybe_send_queue_ack(event, session_key)`` sends
    "📥 Queued (排队中)" and stamps ``_busy_ack_ts`` so the shared 30s
    debounce silences rapid follow-ups (one ACK per session per window).
  * ACK reuses the master ``HERMES_GATEWAY_BUSY_ACK_ENABLED`` gate
    (default true) so users who already disabled all busy ACKs stay
    silent.
  * New per-mode toggle ``HERMES_GATEWAY_BUSY_QUEUE_ACK_ENABLED``
    (default true) and matching ``display.platforms.<platform>.
    busy_queue_ack_enabled`` config key let users opt out per platform
    without touching interrupt/steer ACKs.

Behavior matrix
---------------
  busy_ack_enabled  busy_queue_ack_enabled  | queue-mode ACK
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  true (default)    true (default)          | sent (subject to 30s debounce)
  true              false                   | suppressed
  false             any                     | suppressed (master off)

Tests
-----
Updated tests/gateway/test_busy_session_ack.py:
  * test_busy_text_mode_queue_sends_ack_by_default (new expected behavior)
  * test_busy_text_mode_queue_silent_when_ack_disabled (opt-out via env)
  * test_busy_text_mode_queue_ack_respects_master_switch (master gate)

Old test test_busy_text_mode_queue_delegates_to_adapter_handle_message
(which pinned the pre-fix silent contract) is replaced by the three
above. Full suite: 50/50 pass.

scripts/run-queue-ftests.sh now also runs test_busy_session_ack.py to
catch ACK regressions in the daily cron.

Bug ref: agents/todo/backlog/2026-07-20_020_raw_queue-mode-ack-ux.md
